   372	    Route reachable maroon pixels into several 3x3 destination blocks around red centers.
   373	
   374	    Input structure:
   375	    - The board is an 11x11 floor-and-wall maze with scattered maroon (9) pixels.
   376	    - There are multiple green 3x3 destination blocks, each marked by its own red (2) center.
   377	
   378	    Rule:
   379	    - For every destination block, compute BFS reachability through floor/maroon cells, stopping at walls.
   380	    - Each reachable maroon is owned by the nearest destination block; equal distances break by center row-major order.
   381	    - Every block sorts only its owned maroons by distance and writes them into its own 3x3 cells in row-major order, erasing the moved sources back to floor.
   382	
   383	    Key insight:
   384	    - This is a competitive multi-target collection task, not independent per-block filling.
   385	    - Shared corridors create maroons that more than one block can reach, so you must compare several BFS frontiers first and only then refill each block from its assigned pool.
   386	    """
   387	
   388	    grid = np.asarray(grid, dtype=int)
   389	    h, w = grid.shape
   390	    out = grid.copy()
   391	
   392	    centers = sorted((int(r), int(c)) for r, c in np.argwhere(grid == RED_CENTER))
   393	    assert len(centers) >= 2, "grid must contain multiple red centers"
   394	
   395	    containers = []
   396	    occupied = set()
   397	    for center in centers:
   398	        dest_cells = _dest_cells(center, h, w)
   399	        dest_set = set(dest_cells)
   400	        assert not occupied.intersection(dest_set), "destination blocks must not overlap"
   401	        occupied.update(dest_set)
   402	        containers.append((center, dest_cells, dest_set))
   403	
   404	    floor = _infer_floor(grid)
   405	    passable = {floor, MAROON}
   406	    dists = [_bfs_distance(grid, dest_set, passable) for _, _, dest_set in containers]
   407	
   408	    owned_maroons = [[] for _ in containers]
   409	    for r, c in np.argwhere(grid == MAROON):
   410	        r, c = int(r), int(c)
   411	        owner = _assign_owner(r, c, centers, dists)
   412	        if owner is None:
   413	            continue
   414	        owned_maroons[owner].append((int(dists[owner][r, c]), r, c))
   415	
   416	    for idx, (_, dest_cells, _) in enumerate(containers):
   417	        owned_maroons[idx].sort()
   418	        chosen = owned_maroons[idx][: len(dest_cells)]
   419	        for _, r, c in chosen:
   420	            out[r, c] = floor

